		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Contacts screen]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=148&amp;p=573#p573"><![CDATA[
Thanks to Alex DL4LEX..<br><br>We now have a way to add new Contacts in the OpenGD77 firmware<br><br>There is a new menu item for Contacts with options of "Contact list" and "New contact"<br><br>Both TalkGroup and Private Call  contacts can be added.<br><br>In the Contacts list, the initial display are the TG's . To access the Private Calls, press the # key<br><br>Access to the Contacts list is also available from the CHannel and VFO screens by pressing Function (Blue) + #, and press # to get access the PC list.<br><br>I've uploaded these new features into the OpenGD77_latest.sgl <br><br><a href="https://github.com/rogerclarkmelbourne/OpenGD77/raw/master/firmware_binaries/daily_builds/OpenGD77_latest.sgl" class="postlink">https://github.com/rogerclarkmelbourne/ ... latest.sgl</a><br><br>Specifically this commit to github<br><br><a href="https://github.com/rogerclarkmelbourne/OpenGD77/raw/9281da685fbec75341e2e9b4cb5a0d9a9c957f76/firmware_binaries/daily_builds/OpenGD77_latest.sgl" class="postlink">https://github.com/rogerclarkmelbourne/ ... latest.sgl</a><br><br><br><strong class="text-strong">Note. </strong><br>Although Alex and I have tested this. There is a slight chance it may have bugs, including corrupting your codeplug in the radio<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Fri Nov 22, 2019 11:16 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
